Drop the block signature and post-state root checks from block processing.

Differential testing runs every client with validate_result = false: the block
signature and the post-state root go unchecked while RANDAO, attestation and
the other operation signatures are still verified. Teku has no switch for that
shape -- BLSSignatureVerifier.SIMPLE verifies everything reachable, including
the block signature -- so the two calls are commented out where they are made.

They are commented rather than deleted, next to the reason, because they are
what gets re-enabled if validate_result = true is ever wanted here. The methods
they called stay in the file and pick up @SuppressWarnings("UnusedMethod") so
Error Prone does not fail the build over the now-dead code.
